  "id": "COMPOUND:19803 - PROTEIN:927",
  "verbalization": "Trichilinin D appears to interact with the Alpha-2C adrenergic receptor through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Trichilinin D to the gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit delta, which is targeted by dipropyl-4-hydroxytryptamine, ultimately leading to the Alpha-2C adrenergic receptor. The second and third pathways connect Trichilinin D to inactive dihydropteroate synthase 2, which is targeted by XJHWACIVVQHWBH-JQOAIRLESA-N and religustilide, both of which also target the Alpha-2C adrenergic receptor. These findings suggest that Trichilinin D may exert its effects through different molecular mechanisms, potentially involving diverse signaling pathways that converge on the Alpha-2C adrenergic receptor. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of Trichilinin D's interaction with the receptor, emphasizing the importance of considering multiple targets and their respective mechanisms in understanding its pharmacological profile.",
